# Dependencies
node_modules/

# Build output. The single-file playable is regenerated by `npm run build`, and it inlines
# every asset as base64 — 3.4 MB of generated bytes that would churn on every art change.
# Un-ignore this if a built bundle ever needs to be versioned for handoff.
playable/dist/

# Photoshop authoring files. Deliberately NOT versioned — design.psd alone is 83 MB, and it is
# a binary that churns, so every save would add another full copy to history (or eat the LFS
# quota). Keep it backed up outside the repo.
#
# Consequence to be aware of: layers/ and its manifest.json are the only record of the layout in
# here, so a fresh clone can use the exported art but cannot re-export it from source.
*.psd
*.psb

# Pre-transcode backups of the two layers whose WebP settings were tuned by hand (bg and the
# error vignette). Local safety copies, not sources: the .png beside each one is the source,
# and `npm run art` reproduces the shipped .webp from it. Half a megabyte of redundant binary
# that would churn on every re-encode.
assets/art/layers/_src/

# OS cruft
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
